<QuestionLayout
  title="Is there a performance cost to running the same binary on every OS?"
  description="The portability itself is essentially free — WASM execution runs at near-native speed under Wasmtime on every OS. The real overhead is at the governance boundary: contract validation and trace writing, not the cross-platform part."
